      "closure": "retract-unwitnessed-local-person",
      "independentDisposition": "approve-owner-retraction",
      "sourceRationale": "s0005/zh names 异, 外祖顧歡, and 异祖昭之; s0004/zh names 父巽 (Zhu Xun, p003). Neither unit contains 朱异之母 or an unnamed mother surface. Removing p006 drops a fabricated descriptive-kinship record; maternal grandfather and father remain grounded.",
      "primaryUnits": [
        {
          "unitId": "s0005",
          "zh": "异年數歲，外祖顧歡撫之，謂异祖昭之曰：「此兒非常器，當成卿門戶。」",
          "literalEn": "When Yi was only a few years old, his maternal grandfather Gu Huan dandled him and said to Yi's grandfather Zhao Zhi: \"This boy is no ordinary vessel; he will bring honor to your house.\"",
          "idiomaticEn": "While Yi was still small, his maternal grandfather Gu Huan held him on his knee and told Yi's grandfather Zhao Zhi, \"This child is no common talent—he will uphold your clan.\""
        },
        {
          "unitId": "s0004",
          "zh": "父巽，以義烈知名，官至齊江夏王參軍、吳平令。",
          "literalEn": "His father Xun was famed for righteous valor and reached the posts of Military Aide to the Prince of Jiangxia of Qi and Magistrate of Wuping.",
          "idiomaticEn": "His father Xun won renown for steadfast courage and rose to be an aide to Qi's Prince of Jiangxia and magistrate of Wuping."
        }
      ]
    }
